1
00:00:00,768 --> 00:00:02,048
Sync and ZOTAL
www.zotal.info

2
00:00:02,153 --> 00:00:03,626
(Crow caws)

3
00:00:04,185 --> 00:00:05,251
(Piano playing "Over The River And Through
The Wood") <i>(Frankie) Every family</i>

4
00:00:05,343 --> 00:00:07,535
<i>has their favorite</i>
<i>Thanksgiving recipe.</i>

5
00:00:07,669 --> 00:00:09,218
<i>This is ours.</i>

6
00:00:09,693 --> 00:00:11,320
I just don't get
why we can't stay in a motel.

7
00:00:11,410 --> 00:00:12,995
Because, Mike,

8
00:00:13,087 --> 00:00:16,390
everybody in one house
is what makes holidays special.

9
00:00:16,505 --> 00:00:18,290
Me and my mom and my sister

10
00:00:18,376 --> 00:00:20,790
hanging out in our pj's
having breakfast...

11
00:00:20,887 --> 00:00:24,327
Late nights listening to
my dad tell his bawdy jokes...

12
00:00:24,428 --> 00:00:24,982
Mm.

13
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:26,964
If we stayed at a motel,
we would be missing out

14
00:00:27,055 --> 00:00:29,424
on all those little nuggets
of happiness.

15
00:00:30,202 --> 00:00:33,539
Sorry if I'm not excited about
sleeping on an air mattress.

16
00:00:33,637 --> 00:00:35,363
My back hurts
just thinking about it.

17
00:00:35,447 --> 00:00:38,562
I told you, we get the bedroom
this time. It's our turn.

18
00:00:38,650 --> 00:00:40,534
Besides, Janet won't even
be there till tomorrow

19
00:00:40,636 --> 00:00:43,438
because she's got Lucy's
pilgrim hip-hop recital.

20
00:00:43,525 --> 00:00:46,950
(Scoffs) Great. The miracle
baby's taking hip-hop now?

21
00:00:47,034 --> 00:00:50,928
She <i>was</i> a miracle. Janet had
one good egg, Mike. One.

22
00:00:51,039 --> 00:00:55,273
Oh, yeah. Forgot to tell you.
Aunt Janet called.

23
00:00:55,393 --> 00:00:56,897
She said Lucy's recital
got canceled,

24
00:00:56,987 --> 00:00:58,207
so they're getting there today.

25
00:00:58,358 --> 00:00:59,486
What?

26
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:01,882
(Engine revs)

27
00:01:01,953 --> 00:01:03,586
(Tires screech)

28
00:01:06,547 --> 00:01:08,697
(Mike) Yes! They're not here
yet! Move, move, move!

29
00:01:12,674 --> 00:01:14,877
(Mike) Go, go, go,
go, go, go, go!

30
00:01:17,575 --> 00:01:20,186
(Mike) - Hey!
(Pat) - Ohh...

31
00:01:20,308 --> 00:01:22,278
Happy turkey day, sweetie! Mom!

32
00:01:22,368 --> 00:01:24,267
(Sue) Grandpa!
Hi, pat. Nice to see you.

33
00:01:24,382 --> 00:01:26,658
Good to see you. Good to see you.
How are you, tag?

34
00:01:26,741 --> 00:01:28,191
Aw, come on.
Okay. Here we go.

35
00:01:28,339 --> 00:01:30,140
Oh, you got here fast.

36
00:01:30,283 --> 00:01:31,429
Yeah, we made good time.

37
00:01:31,506 --> 00:01:33,372
I'll, uh, put our stuff
in the bedroom.

38
00:01:33,475 --> 00:01:35,701
(Singsongy) There they are!

39
00:01:35,893 --> 00:01:38,368
Oh, wow, Janet. Oh.
Y-you got here first.

40
00:01:38,467 --> 00:01:39,524
(Normal voice) I know.
We already unpacked.

41
00:01:39,599 --> 00:01:41,164
Gary's in the guest room
getting a little work done

42
00:01:41,221 --> 00:01:45,258
while Lucy takes her nap.
Give your auntie fabulous a hug! (Mouths word)

43
00:01:45,394 --> 00:01:46,932
(Squeals) (Pat) Aw.

44
00:01:47,030 --> 00:01:49,446
Ohh, I miss my <i>sistah.</i>

45
00:01:49,535 --> 00:01:52,168
Ohh.
You look <i>so good.</i>

46
00:01:52,246 --> 00:01:53,544
So when did you guys get here?

47
00:01:53,637 --> 00:01:55,588
Yeah. Yeah, didn't see
your car when we pulled in.

48
00:01:55,692 --> 00:01:57,884
Oh, well, Gary actually
just got a new SUV,

49
00:01:57,972 --> 00:01:59,570
so dad let us
park it in the garage.

50
00:01:59,673 --> 00:02:03,090
Hey, Mike. Come on. I'll get you
set up with them air mattresses.

51
00:02:03,179 --> 00:02:04,024
Oh, no. It's okay, tag.

52
00:02:04,112 --> 00:02:05,571
I remember where they are
from last time.

53
00:02:05,725 --> 00:02:06,759
Oh, shoot. I'm sorry.

54
00:02:06,842 --> 00:02:08,268
Was it your guys' turn
to be in the bedroom?

55
00:02:08,399 --> 00:02:09,762
I just thought
it'd be better for everybody,

56
00:02:09,866 --> 00:02:11,899
you know,
with Lucy's nap time and all,

57
00:02:12,010 --> 00:02:14,152
but we can totally switch
if you want.

58
00:02:14,308 --> 00:02:16,909
(Hissing)

59
00:02:17,676 --> 00:02:18,327
(Sighs)

60
00:02:18,857 --> 00:02:21,990
(Piano playing "Over The River
And Through The Wood")

61
00:02:23,329 --> 00:02:25,210
(Snoring)

62
00:02:30,241 --> 00:02:33,778
Hey, sleepyhead, it's 7:30.
How do you like your tag-cakes?

63
00:02:34,043 --> 00:02:35,020
At 9:30.

64
00:02:35,576 --> 00:02:37,385
(Chuckles)
I'll bet Axl's hungry.

65
00:02:39,613 --> 00:02:40,293
(Munching)

66
00:02:40,381 --> 00:02:41,889
Attaboy. Enjoy 'em.

67
00:02:42,575 --> 00:02:44,634
I put three sticks of butter
in every batch.

68
00:02:44,879 --> 00:02:45,592
Mm.

69
00:02:55,930 --> 00:02:57,969
(Pat) Morning, Mike.
Hey, there he is.

70
00:02:58,069 --> 00:02:59,756
Ooh, you are rocking those pj's.
(Laughs)

71
00:02:59,875 --> 00:03:01,195
Mm-hmm.
(Whistles) Whoo.

72
00:03:02,950 --> 00:03:03,905
(Laughs) So, mom...

73
00:03:04,082 --> 00:03:05,788
What's the plan? When are you
gonna start cooking tomorrow?

74
00:03:05,898 --> 00:03:07,839
Mike's been dreaming about
your famous sweet potatoes.

75
00:03:07,942 --> 00:03:09,582
Oh, don't worry, Mike.

76
00:03:09,702 --> 00:03:12,555
You're gonna get your sweet potatoes.
(Thud)

77
00:03:13,192 --> 00:03:16,908
This year, I prepared everything
ahead of time and I froze it.

78
00:03:17,052 --> 00:03:19,213
Made these babies in July.

79
00:03:19,334 --> 00:03:22,893
After all, Thanksgiving is about
the family, not the food.

80
00:03:23,016 --> 00:03:24,617
It's a little about the food.

81
00:03:24,767 --> 00:03:25,870
- So, mom...
- Mm?

82
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:27,008
You never finished
telling us that story

83
00:03:27,096 --> 00:03:28,554
about Uncle Phil and aunt Helen.

84
00:03:28,679 --> 00:03:31,179
Ooh, yes.
Dirt, <i>ple-ahz.</i>

85
00:03:31,281 --> 00:03:35,107
Well... aunt Helen comes home
early from the bingo trip,

86
00:03:35,210 --> 00:03:38,277
and she found him with
his home health care worker,

87
00:03:38,377 --> 00:03:42,480
proving services not covered
by the HMO. (Gasps)

88
00:03:42,606 --> 00:03:44,188
<i>- No.</i>
- Not again.

89
00:03:44,299 --> 00:03:45,792
Yes, again.

90
00:03:45,935 --> 00:03:48,597
Uh, maybe we should
talk about this later.

91
00:03:48,710 --> 00:03:50,943
It's okay.
Sue can hear the family gossip.

92
00:03:51,034 --> 00:03:53,342
She is not
a little girl anymore.

93
00:03:53,480 --> 00:03:54,845
No, I am not.

94
00:03:55,006 --> 00:03:59,925
I <i>matured</i> on September 21st,
if you know what I'm sayin'.

95
00:04:00,035 --> 00:04:01,447
I'm saying I got my period.
(Laughs)

96
00:04:01,586 --> 00:04:02,650
(Chuckles)

97
00:04:02,743 --> 00:04:03,757
Yeah, we got the e-mail.

98
00:04:03,849 --> 00:04:07,415
So anyway, aunt Helen,
who's still very feisty...

99
00:04:07,512 --> 00:04:08,479
<i>And just like that,</i>

100
00:04:08,588 --> 00:04:11,164
<i>Sue became a member</i>
<i>of the blah blah sisterhood.</i>

101
00:04:11,296 --> 00:04:12,891
(Piano playing "Over The River
And Through The Wood")

102
00:04:16,102 --> 00:04:17,772
Brick, you need
to play with Lucy.

103
00:04:17,893 --> 00:04:21,722
Sue, I'm on vacation.
This is my time to decompress.

104
00:04:21,841 --> 00:04:23,101
Why can't you play with her?

105
00:04:23,196 --> 00:04:25,946
'Cause we adults
are talking in the kitchen,

106
00:04:26,056 --> 00:04:28,187
and she keeps coming in
and interrupting us,

107
00:04:28,319 --> 00:04:29,849
and plus
we're talking about things

108
00:04:29,936 --> 00:04:31,601
that aren't appropriate
for her to hear--

109
00:04:31,719 --> 00:04:34,524
Major family secrets.
I've already said too much.

110
00:04:34,659 --> 00:04:36,550
Okay. Lucy?

111
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:40,323
I'm going into the kitchen with
the adults because I <i>am</i> one.

112
00:04:44,413 --> 00:04:46,098
So...

113
00:04:46,483 --> 00:04:48,212
You want to play librarian?

114
00:04:48,485 --> 00:04:49,953
I'll read, and in six hours,

115
00:04:50,052 --> 00:04:51,623
you tell me
the library's closing.

116
00:04:56,562 --> 00:04:58,244
This one's for my liver.

117
00:04:58,746 --> 00:05:01,682
This one here--
This is for my foot fungus,

118
00:05:01,831 --> 00:05:03,501
and this one thins my blood.

119
00:05:03,695 --> 00:05:05,739
No lie-- If I get
as much as a splinter,

120
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:08,222
I can bleed out faster
than you can say Tom Sawyer.

121
00:05:08,337 --> 00:05:09,131
Heh.

122
00:05:09,271 --> 00:05:10,714
Don't get old, Mike.

123
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:12,918
Believe me,
I'm weighing all my options.

124
00:05:13,063 --> 00:05:14,518
How's that tv coming, Axl?

125
00:05:14,610 --> 00:05:16,306
Yeah, you can
punch those buttons

126
00:05:16,416 --> 00:05:19,203
till you're blue in the face.
That tv ain't coming on.

127
00:05:19,337 --> 00:05:20,867
Damn cable company
wanted to charge me

128
00:05:20,961 --> 00:05:23,880
an extra 4 bucks a month
for HD.

129
00:05:23,992 --> 00:05:26,458
You know where
I told 'em to go.

130
00:05:26,664 --> 00:05:28,191
Here? To fix the tv?

131
00:05:28,287 --> 00:05:30,253
I got those bastards
right where I want 'em.

132
00:05:30,345 --> 00:05:32,941
I guarantee you
they're gonna blink first.

133
00:05:33,068 --> 00:05:35,672
Besides, it's the holidays.
Who needs tv?

134
00:05:35,765 --> 00:05:36,782
- I do.
- I do.

135
00:05:37,410 --> 00:05:39,548
(Gasps) Oh. Janet.
I almost forgot.

136
00:05:39,654 --> 00:05:43,403
I bought the little marshmallows
Lucy wanted for her hot cocoa.

137
00:05:43,517 --> 00:05:44,982
They didn't have the pink ones,

138
00:05:45,072 --> 00:05:46,565
so I just got her
the white ones.

139
00:05:46,659 --> 00:05:49,608
Oh, shoot. She really
wanted the pink ones.

140
00:05:49,735 --> 00:05:51,812
Well, I don't think anybody's
gonna run out right now

141
00:05:51,903 --> 00:05:53,471
just to get a different
color marshmallow.

142
00:05:53,571 --> 00:05:56,319
Can someone run out and get
a different colored marshmallow?

143
00:05:56,491 --> 00:05:57,338
I'll go.

144
00:05:57,428 --> 00:05:58,378
Me, too.

145
00:05:59,101 --> 00:06:00,263
Did you hear
what we're supposed to get?

146
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,970
I just heard
"who wants to leave?"

147
00:06:06,028 --> 00:06:08,075
<i>(Muzak playing)</i>

148
00:06:11,097 --> 00:06:13,425
Hey. How you doing?

149
00:06:14,011 --> 00:06:15,103
Fine.

150
00:06:15,206 --> 00:06:16,946
Cool. <i>Cool.</i>

151
00:06:18,418 --> 00:06:20,301
Just the tiny
pink marshmallows, sir?

152
00:06:20,532 --> 00:06:24,018
Oh, uh... (Clears throat)
Yeah. Right.

153
00:06:24,390 --> 00:06:25,673
Those aren't for me.

154
00:06:25,867 --> 00:06:26,942
Anything else?

155
00:06:27,116 --> 00:06:31,560
Uh, what type of gum
would you recommend?

156
00:06:31,729 --> 00:06:35,885
I, uh, like to chew it
while I play football.

157
00:06:37,267 --> 00:06:39,068
Oh.

158
00:06:39,623 --> 00:06:40,594
Yeah.

159
00:06:40,744 --> 00:06:42,098
Ahh. Hurt my shoulder.

160
00:06:42,247 --> 00:06:44,234
(Inhales sharply) Not sure if it was from football...
(Cash register dings)

161
00:06:44,338 --> 00:06:45,821
Or from playing guitar
in my band that I play in.

162
00:06:46,059 --> 00:06:47,710
You know...

163
00:06:48,914 --> 00:06:50,430
Thank you for shopping
at the mini-mart.

164
00:06:50,714 --> 00:06:53,104
I'm, uh...
Axl, by the way.

165
00:06:53,186 --> 00:06:55,271
Thank you, Axl,
for shopping at the mini-mart.

166
00:07:01,647 --> 00:07:03,579
(Chuckles) What?

167
00:07:04,433 --> 00:07:05,029
Nothing.

168
00:07:05,119 --> 00:07:07,862
I just never really witnessed
your game up close before.

169
00:07:08,207 --> 00:07:09,878
(Imitating Axl) "What kind
of gum would you recommend?"

170
00:07:09,991 --> 00:07:11,314
Hey, I think I laid
some nice groundwork.

171
00:07:11,416 --> 00:07:14,911
Really? 'Cause I think you dug
a big hole and then fell in it.

172
00:07:15,065 --> 00:07:16,956
You can't just talk
about yourself, Axl.

173
00:07:17,062 --> 00:07:18,781
You gotta ask them
some questions.

174
00:07:19,035 --> 00:07:20,783
Women like to talk
about themselves.

175
00:07:21,172 --> 00:07:23,472
Why do you even care about this?
'Cause someday

176
00:07:23,573 --> 00:07:25,991
I'd like you to get married
and get out of my house.

177
00:07:28,203 --> 00:07:30,567
(Lucy cries)

178
00:07:31,447 --> 00:07:32,386
Ohh.

179
00:07:32,495 --> 00:07:33,685
He won again!

180
00:07:33,830 --> 00:07:38,183
<i>I</i> wanted to be
the pretty pretty princess!

181
00:07:38,285 --> 00:07:40,374
Pumpkin, did you?
(Cries)

182
00:07:40,528 --> 00:07:43,218
Did you want to be
the pretty pretty princess?

183
00:07:43,334 --> 00:07:44,491
Uhuh. (Crying)

184
00:07:44,570 --> 00:07:46,517
You know, Frankie, it wouldn't
kill Brick to let her win.

185
00:07:46,624 --> 00:07:49,115
Mom, look at me.

186
00:07:49,237 --> 00:07:52,863
Do you honestly think
I wanted to win this game?

187
00:07:52,981 --> 00:07:54,785
Whatever, Brick.
Just pick something she can win.

188
00:07:54,883 --> 00:07:56,589
I tried letting her win
at connect four,

189
00:07:56,702 --> 00:07:58,691
but she literally
couldn't connect four

190
00:07:58,798 --> 00:08:01,164
and I couldn't stop
connecting four.

191
00:08:01,323 --> 00:08:03,346
(Lowered voice)
You know, for a miracle baby,

192
00:08:03,476 --> 00:08:04,913
she's not too bright.

193
00:08:05,033 --> 00:08:06,896
(Lucy cries)

194
00:08:08,124 --> 00:08:11,221
Wow. Brick's a little
competitive there, isn't he?

195
00:08:11,333 --> 00:08:12,952
I guess he's just
not used to this.

196
00:08:13,086 --> 00:08:15,798
At our house, if you win, you
win, and if you lose, you lose.

197
00:08:15,948 --> 00:08:18,129
You know,
kind of like in real life.

198
00:08:18,253 --> 00:08:20,621
That's funny, 'cause a lot
of the books that I'm reading

199
00:08:20,716 --> 00:08:23,386
are kind of saying
the opposite of that, so...

200
00:08:25,069 --> 00:08:26,280
Hey, you know what?

201
00:08:26,344 --> 00:08:27,786
There's a lot of snow outside,

202
00:08:27,873 --> 00:08:29,612
so you kids want to
go out and play in it?

203
00:08:29,703 --> 00:08:30,863
Brick loves building snowmen.

204
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,810
He does?

205
00:08:33,082 --> 00:08:35,221
(Babyish voice)
Do you want to build a snowman

206
00:08:35,318 --> 00:08:37,180
with your cousin, sweetie?

207
00:08:37,333 --> 00:08:38,612
Get outside, Brick.

208
00:08:38,756 --> 00:08:41,127
(Piano playing "Over The River
And Through The Wood")

209
00:08:45,891 --> 00:08:49,099
(Crying) It's okay, puppy.

210
00:08:49,379 --> 00:08:51,560
(Sighs)
We can't find Mr. Bear.

211
00:08:51,719 --> 00:08:53,331
Probably went someplace
with the tv.

212
00:08:53,447 --> 00:08:55,418
Lucy goose, we'll find him.

213
00:08:55,540 --> 00:08:56,904
(Crying)

214
00:08:56,999 --> 00:09:00,615
It's okay. Mr. Bear will
turn up. Let's not freak out.

215
00:09:00,791 --> 00:09:01,961
She's not freaking out.

216
00:09:02,053 --> 00:09:02,977
She's just upset, which is

217
00:09:03,095 --> 00:09:06,150
an appropriate emotional
response for the situation.

218
00:09:06,284 --> 00:09:07,323
Okay.

219
00:09:07,575 --> 00:09:08,564
How about this?

220
00:09:08,744 --> 00:09:10,628
Why don't we calm down
and have a little snack?

221
00:09:11,022 --> 00:09:12,103
And we'll look for him later.

222
00:09:12,312 --> 00:09:13,876
Does that sound okay
to you, Lucy?

223
00:09:17,290 --> 00:09:18,506
Is this one of those
nuggets of happiness

224
00:09:18,597 --> 00:09:19,868
you were talking about?

225
00:09:20,349 --> 00:09:22,614
And by the way,
why the hell isn't Gary out here

226
00:09:22,716 --> 00:09:24,376
enjoying this nugget with us?

227
00:09:24,521 --> 00:09:26,672
Because he's
in his room working.

228
00:09:26,834 --> 00:09:29,379
He's a chiropractor.

229
00:09:29,604 --> 00:09:31,531
What could he possibly
be working on?

230
00:09:31,958 --> 00:09:33,137
(Axl) Found it!

231
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:40,289
Ohh. That was really scary, huh?

232
00:09:40,428 --> 00:09:42,697
I hope you never have to
go through anything like that

233
00:09:42,804 --> 00:09:43,877
ever again.

234
00:09:44,131 --> 00:09:45,080
(Squeak)

235
00:09:45,206 --> 00:09:47,933
<i>(Distorted male voice)</i>
<i>I love you.</i>

236
00:09:48,058 --> 00:09:49,625
Whoa.
Mr. bear's stroking out.

237
00:09:51,108 --> 00:09:55,896
He's broken. It's Brick's fault.
He had it last!

238
00:09:56,025 --> 00:09:56,963
No, I didn't.

239
00:09:57,102 --> 00:09:58,622
I came in to get hot cocoa,

240
00:09:58,720 --> 00:10:01,046
- and you were still playing with him.
- I was not!

241
00:10:01,159 --> 00:10:03,279
Why don't you kids
come to the kitchen?

242
00:10:03,378 --> 00:10:05,977
And grandma will
defrost you some cookies.

243
00:10:07,119 --> 00:10:10,101
Ohh. It's just such a bummer,
'cause it was her favorite toy.

244
00:10:10,208 --> 00:10:11,279
Oh, she'll get over it.

245
00:10:11,352 --> 00:10:13,227
Stick a couple cookies
in her mouth, she'll be fine.

246
00:10:13,402 --> 00:10:15,680
Yeah, it's just so unlike Lucy
to leave a toy outside.

247
00:10:15,765 --> 00:10:17,550
She's usually really,
really responsible.

248
00:10:17,666 --> 00:10:19,691
Kids-- What are you
gonna do, right?

249
00:10:19,795 --> 00:10:20,692
Right.

250
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:22,239
Anyway, the bear was $60,

251
00:10:22,354 --> 00:10:24,593
and you can get him
at the toy store at the mall.

252
00:10:28,160 --> 00:10:28,940
(Sighs)

253
00:10:30,549 --> 00:10:34,364
(Piano playing "Over The River
And Through The Wood")

254
00:10:34,906 --> 00:10:36,356
Mike, are you awake?

255
00:10:36,447 --> 00:10:37,602
What do you think?

256
00:10:37,703 --> 00:10:40,046
I really think Janet wants me
to pay for that bear.

257
00:10:40,255 --> 00:10:41,225
That's 'cause she does.

258
00:10:41,394 --> 00:10:43,023
(Sighs) I can't believe
she could act this way.

259
00:10:43,111 --> 00:10:45,085
I just think it's so wrong.

260
00:10:45,183 --> 00:10:46,116
So tell her that.

261
00:10:46,216 --> 00:10:48,057
Oh, maybe I should
just give her the money.

262
00:10:48,157 --> 00:10:49,179
Sounds great.

263
00:10:49,353 --> 00:10:52,273
No. You know what?
I'm not giving her the money.

264
00:10:52,357 --> 00:10:52,813
Mm.

265
00:10:52,903 --> 00:10:54,603
She and Gary
are doing very well,

266
00:10:54,715 --> 00:10:57,268
and she knows we couldn't
even afford to fix our roof.

267
00:10:57,368 --> 00:11:00,129
We can't afford
to just throw away 60 bucks.

268
00:11:00,229 --> 00:11:03,455
I will give you 75 right now
to stop this conversation.

269
00:11:03,591 --> 00:11:04,606
You know what makes me mad?

270
00:11:04,693 --> 00:11:08,201
Well, it's not waking up
your husband. That's for sure.

271
00:11:08,330 --> 00:11:09,921
She's questioning
our son's honesty.

272
00:11:10,029 --> 00:11:12,469
Brick said he didn't do it,
he didn't do it.

273
00:11:12,582 --> 00:11:14,169
He didn't do it, did he?

274
00:11:14,284 --> 00:11:16,429
(Brick) I didn't do it.

275
00:11:16,553 --> 00:11:18,049
Brick, this is
a private conversation.

276
00:11:18,151 --> 00:11:19,634
- No, it's not.
- Wish it was.

277
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:20,510
I didn't do it.

278
00:11:20,601 --> 00:11:23,277
Hey, hey. Everybody pipe down.
It's almost 6:00 in the morning.

279
00:11:23,387 --> 00:11:24,844
I'd like to get
two seconds' sleep

280
00:11:24,935 --> 00:11:27,260
before the sun comes up
on another tv-less day.

281
00:11:28,229 --> 00:11:29,200
(Curtain rings swoosh)

282
00:11:29,367 --> 00:11:31,132
Happy Thanksgiving!

283
00:11:31,636 --> 00:11:33,368
(All groaning)

284
00:11:33,752 --> 00:11:34,802
(Switch clicks)

285
00:11:34,951 --> 00:11:36,455
<i>With even his own family</i>
<i>doubting him,</i>

286
00:11:36,574 --> 00:11:39,104
<i>Brick knew it was to him</i>
<i>to prove his innocence.</i>

287
00:11:45,349 --> 00:11:47,356
Uh, the defrosting
seems to have

288
00:11:47,446 --> 00:11:49,026
sucked a little taste
out of the food

289
00:11:49,153 --> 00:11:50,862
and tag's
used up all the butter,

290
00:11:50,969 --> 00:11:52,946
so I'm gonna need someone
to run to the store.

291
00:11:53,125 --> 00:11:54,771
- Got it.
- On it.

292
00:11:57,900 --> 00:11:58,598
(Door closes)

293
00:11:58,934 --> 00:12:00,643
Ooh, Brick, can you be
careful with that frame?

294
00:12:00,754 --> 00:12:02,140
That's one of
grandma's favorites.

295
00:12:02,327 --> 00:12:04,110
He can pick up
the frame, Janet.

296
00:12:04,247 --> 00:12:05,848
Oh, okay, sure.

297
00:12:05,993 --> 00:12:08,568
But remember that one time when
he broke mom's antique vase?

298
00:12:08,695 --> 00:12:11,480
That was when he was 5.
He's 10 now. He's fine.

299
00:12:11,669 --> 00:12:13,509
Sure, but he still
has his issues, right?

300
00:12:13,643 --> 00:12:15,290
What do you mean, issues?

301
00:12:15,434 --> 00:12:18,558
Well, you know, he's got
his things. He's, like, special.

302
00:12:18,730 --> 00:12:21,354
Brick's not special.
He's perfectly normal.

303
00:12:21,478 --> 00:12:23,857
Don't worry about anything,
Brick. You're fine.

304
00:12:24,979 --> 00:12:25,959
(Clink)

305
00:12:30,980 --> 00:12:31,544
<i>(Muzak playing)</i>

306
00:12:31,635 --> 00:12:32,167
Okay.

307
00:12:32,255 --> 00:12:33,291
Watch and learn.

308
00:12:33,379 --> 00:12:34,326
(Sighs)

309
00:12:36,199 --> 00:12:37,920
So they got you working
on Thanksgiving, huh?

310
00:12:38,108 --> 00:12:40,870
Yeah, but it's okay. I'm trying
to save some money for college.

311
00:12:40,931 --> 00:12:42,485
Oh, is that right?
What high school do you go to?

312
00:12:42,595 --> 00:12:43,469
St. Mary's.

313
00:12:43,576 --> 00:12:45,742
Oh, yeah. That's the catholic
school just down the street.

314
00:12:45,845 --> 00:12:48,943
So do you gotta wear
those catholic girl uniforms

315
00:12:49,041 --> 00:12:50,032
with the skirts?

316
00:12:52,132 --> 00:12:55,052
Sir, this conversation
is making me uncomfortable.

317
00:13:00,483 --> 00:13:01,792
Smooth, dad.

318
00:13:01,897 --> 00:13:04,701
I thought that "Dateline" guy
was gonna come out of the back.

319
00:13:04,811 --> 00:13:05,493
(Chuckles) Shut up.

320
00:13:11,114 --> 00:13:12,541
Hey, guys, you got the butter?

321
00:13:12,680 --> 00:13:14,579
Actually, they were out.

322
00:13:14,751 --> 00:13:18,379
Out? I buy 12 sticks
a week there.

323
00:13:18,496 --> 00:13:20,703
Come on. I'll come with you
and show you where they are.

324
00:13:21,860 --> 00:13:22,886
(Axl sighs)

325
00:13:24,072 --> 00:13:25,240
Hey, guys.

326
00:13:25,393 --> 00:13:26,687
Where's the fire?

327
00:13:27,159 --> 00:13:28,592
We're going to the store
to get butter.

328
00:13:28,711 --> 00:13:32,102
Interesting.

329
00:13:32,733 --> 00:13:33,839
Now is there a reason

330
00:13:33,952 --> 00:13:36,580
why it takes three adults
to purchase dairy products?

331
00:13:36,812 --> 00:13:39,261
It would only take one adult
to stuff you in a snowbank.

332
00:13:41,081 --> 00:13:42,351
Okay.

333
00:13:43,010 --> 00:13:44,344
Just don't leave town.

334
00:13:48,725 --> 00:13:52,318
(Piano playing "Over The River
And Through The Wood")

335
00:13:53,272 --> 00:13:56,473
So I think she wants me
to buy her a new bear.

336
00:13:56,621 --> 00:13:59,018
Did she say that?

337
00:13:59,116 --> 00:14:01,926
Well, not exactly,
but you know her tone, mom.

338
00:14:02,029 --> 00:14:03,173
There was a definite tone.

339
00:14:03,262 --> 00:14:06,643
And it's not even the money that
bothers me. It's the judgment.

340
00:14:06,764 --> 00:14:10,108
I'm just happy to have both
my girls home for the holiday.

341
00:14:11,171 --> 00:14:13,180
(Lowered voice) I'm just saying,
since he's the one who broke it,

342
00:14:13,289 --> 00:14:15,961
they should step up
and, you know, pay for--

343
00:14:16,070 --> 00:14:16,946
(Normal voice) Hey.

344
00:14:17,018 --> 00:14:18,280
Hey. What are you guys
talking about?

345
00:14:18,367 --> 00:14:21,497
Oh. We were just discussing
how to prepare the corn.

346
00:14:21,654 --> 00:14:22,670
Oh, really?

347
00:14:22,776 --> 00:14:24,125
- Mm-hmm.
- 'Cause the corn is my job.

348
00:14:24,238 --> 00:14:25,904
So if the corn is being
discussed, it's sort of weird

349
00:14:26,010 --> 00:14:28,258
that I'm not part of
the corn discussion, isn't it?

350
00:14:37,593 --> 00:14:38,998
All right, Axl.
Go get the butter.

351
00:14:39,114 --> 00:14:40,316
Well, why can't you do it?

352
00:14:40,448 --> 00:14:42,022
'Cause I don't want to.

353
00:14:43,470 --> 00:14:44,787
Hey, guys, what gives?

354
00:14:44,885 --> 00:14:45,713
He doesn't want
to go back in there

355
00:14:45,796 --> 00:14:48,180
'cause he got shot down trying
to pick up the hot cashier.

356
00:14:48,293 --> 00:14:50,324
No, I was trying to teach him
how to talk to girls

357
00:14:50,447 --> 00:14:52,262
'cause he was
embarrassing himself.

358
00:14:52,362 --> 00:14:55,860
(Chuckles) Axl, Axl, Axl.

359
00:14:55,998 --> 00:14:58,075
Listen, if you wanted tips
on the ladies,

360
00:14:58,172 --> 00:15:00,130
you should have come
to the old tag-eroo.

361
00:15:00,291 --> 00:15:03,566
Here's what you do.
First you win over her father.

362
00:15:03,693 --> 00:15:06,741
Then you buy her a rose
every day for two weeks.

363
00:15:06,858 --> 00:15:10,699
Trust me, you'll be
holding hands in six months.

364
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:13,365
Well, grandpa, that's all
really awesome advi--

365
00:15:13,469 --> 00:15:15,653
Come on, let's go in.
I'll be your sidecar.

366
00:15:15,749 --> 00:15:16,725
Wingman.

367
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:18,188
(Sighs)

368
00:15:20,923 --> 00:15:22,773
<i>(Muzak playing)</i>

369
00:15:28,038 --> 00:15:29,334
Hi there.

370
00:15:31,205 --> 00:15:34,148
Still selling
those gummi worms, huh?

371
00:15:34,627 --> 00:15:35,879
Yeah.

372
00:15:36,166 --> 00:15:40,937
Classic candy. 'Couse my wife
won't let me eat 'em anymore.

373
00:15:41,045 --> 00:15:42,471
They-- they give me the winds.

374
00:15:50,703 --> 00:15:51,789
(Sighs)

375
00:15:55,354 --> 00:15:58,239
(Piano playing "Over The River
And Through The Wood")

376
00:15:59,519 --> 00:16:00,621
Hey.

377
00:16:01,140 --> 00:16:02,397
Are you sleeping?

378
00:16:02,528 --> 00:16:04,265
I'm just trying
to take a little nap.

379
00:16:04,611 --> 00:16:05,613
Oh. Okay.

380
00:16:05,720 --> 00:16:08,432
Just because you said you were
gonna do the corn, so...

381
00:16:08,596 --> 00:16:11,380
Yeah. I'm a little tired.

382
00:16:11,481 --> 00:16:14,334
I haven't been getting much
sleep down here in my <i>bedroom.</i>

383
00:16:14,474 --> 00:16:16,505
You know what?
I offered to give you

384
00:16:16,594 --> 00:16:17,845
the guest room
when you got here.

385
00:16:17,972 --> 00:16:20,942
Oh, yeah.
It was a nice offer.

386
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:23,139
"Oh, I just thought
it would be best for everybody,

387
00:16:23,238 --> 00:16:25,088
you know,
with Lucy's naps."

388
00:16:25,215 --> 00:16:28,181
For your information,
Lucy's pediatrician said

389
00:16:28,276 --> 00:16:30,407
she needs a quiet environment
to sleep in.

390
00:16:30,541 --> 00:16:32,938
Oh, really?
She doesn't sleep well?

391
00:16:33,068 --> 00:16:33,659
Yeah.

392
00:16:33,769 --> 00:16:34,832
'Cause I thought
the miracle baby

393
00:16:34,935 --> 00:16:37,597
just hovered over her bed
on a magical cloud.

394
00:16:37,716 --> 00:16:40,577
Ohh. And there it is.
You know what?

395
00:16:40,682 --> 00:16:42,326
You have always resented Lucy

396
00:16:42,421 --> 00:16:46,417
because you never wanted another
mom having a reason to be tired.

397
00:16:46,556 --> 00:16:47,667
What?!

398
00:16:47,789 --> 00:16:50,135
<i>Ohh,</i> you're always
<i>so</i> worn out, Frankie,

399
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:52,225
and you love it
because you're a martyr.

400
00:16:52,325 --> 00:16:53,675
Every time I call you
on the phone,

401
00:16:53,780 --> 00:16:56,176
you never have time to talk
because you're <i>so overwhelmed.</i>

402
00:16:56,287 --> 00:16:58,886
Well, guess what?
I'm tired, too!

403
00:16:59,046 --> 00:17:00,693
<i>You</i> think you're
more tired than <i>me?</i>

404
00:17:00,789 --> 00:17:02,251
Yeah, I know that I am.
As a matter of fact,

405
00:17:02,348 --> 00:17:04,704
maybe I'll just lie around now,
too. How about that?

406
00:17:05,934 --> 00:17:07,308
Oh, no. No.

407
00:17:07,447 --> 00:17:09,928
How could <i>you</i> be tired?
You've got one kid.

408
00:17:10,067 --> 00:17:11,492
(Sighs) I've got three!

409
00:17:11,607 --> 00:17:14,795
Not to mention a full-time job
and a house to keep clean.

410
00:17:14,911 --> 00:17:16,463
Oh, right. You're all about
the clean house.

411
00:17:16,558 --> 00:17:18,097
Look, we're just about
to have Thanksgiving dinner,

412
00:17:18,210 --> 00:17:20,345
and it looks like
a <i>bomb</i> got dropped in here.

413
00:17:20,442 --> 00:17:23,750
You want me to clean up?
Fine. Fine. I'll clean up.

414
00:17:23,857 --> 00:17:25,743
Here. Here we go.
I'm cleaning the hell up!

415
00:17:25,838 --> 00:17:27,411
- Is that clean enough for you?
- Perfect!

416
00:17:27,532 --> 00:17:29,081
Maybe I'll even make my bed.

417
00:17:29,180 --> 00:17:30,681
Hey, there's a first time
for everything.

418
00:17:30,794 --> 00:17:33,957
- Get off!
- No! I'm tired. I'm resting.

419
00:17:34,071 --> 00:17:35,513
Get off, Janet!

420
00:17:35,627 --> 00:17:36,606
Make me!

421
00:17:38,282 --> 00:17:40,078
(Grunting)

422
00:17:40,175 --> 00:17:40,839
(Pants) Listen.

423
00:17:40,929 --> 00:17:43,615
Lucy happens to be very gifted,
and it's a lot of work.

424
00:17:43,711 --> 00:17:45,630
There's dance and French...

425
00:17:45,698 --> 00:17:48,189
Your kids are almost grown up.
How hard could that be?

426
00:17:48,285 --> 00:17:49,225
(Yells)

427
00:17:49,602 --> 00:17:52,705
You think this is all
smooth sailing for me?!

428
00:17:52,814 --> 00:17:53,627
Huh?!

429
00:17:53,745 --> 00:17:56,197
Do you know what I found
in Axl's bed the other week?

430
00:17:56,357 --> 00:17:58,689
A gallon
of chocolate chip ice cream.

431
00:17:58,786 --> 00:18:00,223
Sue cannot make a team
to save her life,

432
00:18:00,315 --> 00:18:02,864
and on top of all of that,
Brick is special!

433
00:18:02,984 --> 00:18:04,585
Oh. So now Brick's special.

434
00:18:04,700 --> 00:18:05,983
Because before
you said he wasn't.

435
00:18:06,090 --> 00:18:07,759
So maybe you should get
two different flags to hold up

436
00:18:07,842 --> 00:18:09,852
so we know which Brick
you're talking about!

437
00:18:09,958 --> 00:18:11,201
(Both pant)

438
00:18:11,364 --> 00:18:15,506
I'm not paying
for that stupid bear!

439
00:18:15,659 --> 00:18:20,302
Fine! Forget about it!
I'll pay for the bear!

440
00:18:20,397 --> 00:18:21,226
How about this?

441
00:18:21,327 --> 00:18:22,989
I'll buy you a new bear
when you replace

442
00:18:23,098 --> 00:18:26,533
that plastic hot dog you lost
from my picnic set when I was 6!

443
00:18:26,642 --> 00:18:28,681
Mom bought that for both of us!

444
00:18:28,776 --> 00:18:33,000
Not true!
It... was... <i>Mine!</i>

445
00:18:33,348 --> 00:18:34,344
(Thud) Uhh!

446
00:18:34,442 --> 00:18:35,125
(Yelling)

447
00:18:35,285 --> 00:18:36,417
(Thud) Uhh!

448
00:18:39,578 --> 00:18:40,644
(Sighs)

449
00:18:42,149 --> 00:18:45,352
<i>What followed was the quietest</i>
<i>Thanksgiving dinner ever.</i>

450
00:18:45,629 --> 00:18:48,865
<i>No talking-- Just the sound</i>
<i>of plastic on paper.</i>

451
00:18:49,059 --> 00:18:51,959
<i>But for Brick,</i>
<i>there was a mystery to solve,</i>

452
00:18:52,047 --> 00:18:54,167
<i>so he did what</i>
<i>any good detective would do.</i>

453
00:18:54,369 --> 00:18:56,094
<i>He returned</i>
<i>to the scene of the crime.</i>

454
00:18:57,947 --> 00:18:59,281
Note--

455
00:18:59,711 --> 00:19:02,706
Two sets of footprints lead
to where the bear was found.

456
00:19:02,832 --> 00:19:05,502
One are Axl's,
who found the furry victim.

457
00:19:05,655 --> 00:19:09,663
The other ones have
a star pattern on the bottom.

458
00:19:11,327 --> 00:19:14,414
Clearly, whoever has a star
on the bottom of their boots

459
00:19:14,533 --> 00:19:15,666
is the culprit.

460
00:19:16,087 --> 00:19:17,855
(Whispers) Culprit.

461
00:19:23,570 --> 00:19:25,907
I'm finding
multiple star footprints.

462
00:19:27,306 --> 00:19:30,065
Oh, my gosh.
They're following me.

463
00:19:38,297 --> 00:19:39,328
<i>And with that,</i>

464
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:42,094
<i>Inspector Whodunit</i>
<i>closed the case.</i>

465
00:19:42,594 --> 00:19:46,038
(Piano playing "Over The River
And Through The Wood")

466
00:19:48,953 --> 00:19:50,520
(Bottles clink)

467
00:19:53,560 --> 00:19:55,230
Is there any stuffing in there?

468
00:20:02,305 --> 00:20:03,731
(Voice breaking) I'm so sorry.

469
00:20:03,823 --> 00:20:05,195
I'm sorry, too.

470
00:20:05,291 --> 00:20:05,938
Ohh.

471
00:20:06,076 --> 00:20:08,167
I didn't mean
all those things I said.

472
00:20:08,246 --> 00:20:09,253
Oh, neither did I.

473
00:20:09,369 --> 00:20:10,992
You know, I think
the reason we fight

474
00:20:11,105 --> 00:20:14,057
is because
we love each other so much,

475
00:20:14,148 --> 00:20:15,861
but we never get
to see each other.

476
00:20:15,968 --> 00:20:17,468
We need to get together more.

477
00:20:17,588 --> 00:20:19,531
Yeah.
That's what needs to happen.

478
00:20:19,679 --> 00:20:23,795
And I'm sorry if I make you feel
like I don't have time for you.

479
00:20:23,908 --> 00:20:26,708
I think sometimes I want
to get off the phone because

480
00:20:26,837 --> 00:20:31,521
I'm jealous that your life
seems to be going all perfect.

481
00:20:31,637 --> 00:20:33,900
Oh, no, silly, I'm not perfect.

482
00:20:34,034 --> 00:20:37,203
It's just easier for me.
I could never do what you do.

483
00:20:37,308 --> 00:20:38,122
Oh, stop.

484
00:20:38,217 --> 00:20:40,699
No, it's true, Frankie.
Don't you understand?

485
00:20:40,787 --> 00:20:42,149
Watching you as a mom
was the whole reason

486
00:20:42,248 --> 00:20:44,420
I wanted to have kids
in the first place.

487
00:20:44,544 --> 00:20:45,338
Oh!

488
